<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H1615</pnldref><english><title>Permit the failure to keep company accounts - proper place</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>COMPANIES ACT 1985</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>222</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>PERMIT</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>PERMITTING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>PERMISSION</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>ACCOUNTING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>KNOWINGLY</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>WILFULLY</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DEFAULT</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being an officer of **(..SPECIFY COMPANY..), knowingly and wilfully permitted default to be made by the company under Section&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(A)_[222(1)]_&lt;br /&gt;(B)_[222(2)]_&lt;br /&gt;(C)_[222(3)]_&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;of the Companies Act 1985 in that **(..SPECIFY PARTICULARS..)</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 222(4) of and Schedule 24 to the Companies Act 1985.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt; officer of company&lt;br /&gt; knowingly/wilfully authorise default by company &lt;br /&gt; under Subsections 222(1)/(2) or (3)</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>Repealed by s.1295 and Sch 16 Companies Act 2006&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(i) Subsection 222(1) relates to the keeping of records at the registered office of the company and open to inspection.&lt;br /&gt;(ii) Subsection 222(2) relates to accounts and returns being sent to Great Britain where records are kept abroad.&lt;br /&gt;(iii) Subsection 222(3) deals with the content of those returns.&lt;br /&gt;(iv) See Section 730(5) for meaning of 'officer in default'.&lt;br /&gt;(v) See also the associated offence wording as follows: H1614.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>Complex - see legislation</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>SUMMARY: Six months imprisonment and / or a fine not exceeding the statutory max